{
  "_comment": [
    "The seven public plans. Single source of truth shared by the plain-JS",
    "versioned seeder (which runs under bare node in the production image) and",
    "the TypeScript spec that guards this matrix.",
    "",
    "monthlyMinor/yearlyMinor are integer MINOR units ($5.00 => 500).",
    "daily/weekly/monthlyTokens are cost-normalized weighted tokens:",
    "1,000,000 weighted tokens == $1.00 of estimated provider cost.",
    "costCeilingMicroUsd is a STRING because it is converted to BigInt — an",
    "internal profitability control that is never returned to a normal user.",
    "null means unlimited; 0 means disabled. They are never interchangeable.",
    "",
    "monthlyTokens and costCeilingMicroUsd are DELIBERATELY IDENTICAL per plan.",
    "1 weighted token == 1 micro-USD (WEIGHTED_TOKENS_PER_USD ===",
    "MICRO_USD_PER_USD), so they are one number wearing two names, and the",
    "PAYG wallet grants exactly that number each period (ADR-078). Letting them",
    "drift would let the smaller of the two bind and refuse a user at half the",
    "credit their billing page shows.",
    "",
    "These numbers apply to FRESH INSTALLS ONLY. An existing install is moved",
    "by prisma/seeders/plan-payg-allowance.seeder.js, which only rewrites rows",
    "still holding the OLD value so an operator's tuned figure survives. Do NOT",
    "bump plan-catalog to v3 to apply them: on an install where v2 already ran,",
    "every plan takes the else-branch of run() and only modelAccessMode and a",
    "null weeklyTokenQuota are written — the new allowances would land on ZERO",
    "rows while the seeder reported success."
  ],
